  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1226 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nVery little changes from previous forecasts. Mostly dry and warm \nconditions are expected for most of the forecast with only a low \nchance for showers Monday. Better rain chances return to the \nforecast late next as we head into next weekend. Although we will \nnot get any direct impacts from Hurricane Isaias, long period swells \nare expected through the end of the week are expected to interact \nwith Ekman Transport to promote coastal flooding. Coastal flooding \nand high risk of rip currents are expected to continue through the \nweekend with coastal flooding even possible at time low tide \nperiods. \n\nWarm temperatures return with highs in the 90s through the week into \nnext week. Moisture will increase next week with heat index values \nover 105 degrees returning along with a moderate to major risk of \nheat-related impacts Monday. Please remember to continue to practice \nheat safety: take breaks when outside, drink plenty of water, and \nlook before you lock.",
